                <pb facs="0721" n="689" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v13/pg689"/>

                <head>390. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>During the evening of September 10, the Department of State transmitted to
                    certain Middle Eastern posts a series of messages to be delivered orally to
                    Prime Minister Ben Gurion, Prime Minister Menderes, Crown Prince Abdul-illah
                    (who was then in Turkey), President Chamoun and Foreign Minister Malik, and King
                    Hussein. (See <ref target="#d391">Documents 391</ref>–<ref target="#d394"
                        >394</ref>) Secretary Dulles discussed drafts of the messages with
                    Ambassador Caccia on September 8 and 10. During <pb facs="0722" n="690"
                        xml:id="pg690"/> the latter conversation, Caccia conveyed comments on the
                    drafts which he had received from the British Foreign Office. (Memorandum of
                    conversation by Dulles, September 8; Department of State, S/S Files: Lot 66 D
                    123; Memorandum of conversation by Rockwell, September 10; Eisenhower Library,
                    Dulles Papers, S/Miss Bernau)</p>
            </div>
